      "content": "That summary sounds like a good start for the lesson plan. To make the curriculum more robust, could you flesh out those specific rhetorical frameworks you mentioned? Specifically, can you explain the \"logic\" behind the concept of the \"White Man's Burden\" as it was understood by those administrators? I'm interested in how they framed their presence as a moral obligation or a \"duty\" to handle certain social and political aspects of those regions. It would be helpful to see those specific thematic arguments laid out so I can teach my students how to identify these patterns of paternalism in historical texts.",
